--state-root DIR: the sandbox's $HOME and /tmp backed by DIR/home and DIR/tmp
on disk instead of tmpfs, and DIR/claude as CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR unless
--claude-dir names one. DIR and its children must be absolute, not symlinks,
owned by the caller and not group/world writable; missing parts are created
0700. Linux only, refused under --lockdown, never saved to a profile.

From the zeo-workspace/ai-jail fork, branch feat/state-root (on upstream
v3.5.0), applied here on top of the resource-limits patch. Zeo's per-project
jail uses it (Zeo next proposal §6.54).

